# Pump encoding, DOLCE (pins: appliedontolab/DOLCE @ 0e059fd).
#
# R1: the impeller is part of the pump during the interval t1 -- asserted
# through the reified temporary-parthood pattern of DOLCEnaryRel: one
# individual of RRelTempPart carrying part, whole, and time. That the
# parthood lives in a reified individual rather than in a binary relation
# is the Section 6.1.2 finding this file makes concrete; the module's
# presence chains project presence from the reification, and by design
# nothing projects to a timeless binary parthood (see probes/dolce/).
#
# The class and property declarations below repeat what the pinned
# modules already declare, so the file renders correctly when opened on
# its own (in Protege, undeclared properties display as annotations).
# No semantics are repeated: chains, transitivity, and the rest come
# only from DOLCEbasic.owl and DOLCEnaryRel.owl at the pin.
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix basic: <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#> .
@prefix nary:  <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEnaryRel#> .
@prefix p:     <https://example.org/mt-pump#> .

basic:PhysicalObject a owl:Class .
basic:TimeInterval   a owl:Class .
nary:RRelTempPart    a owl:Class .
nary:tempPart  a owl:ObjectProperty .
nary:tempWhole a owl:ObjectProperty .
nary:rRelTime  a owl:ObjectProperty .

p:pump     a basic:PhysicalObject .
p:impeller a basic:PhysicalObject .
p:t1       a basic:TimeInterval .

p:r1 a nary:RRelTempPart ;
    nary:tempPart  p:impeller ;
    nary:tempWhole p:pump ;
    nary:rRelTime  p:t1 .

# R2: the impeller-housing joint is inexpressible. DOLCE's artifact (and
# theory) carries no connection or contact vocabulary; the absence check
# is recorded in results/inventory.txt.
